# Heretic + Watermarks-Remover Deep Analysis

Spec: DeepAnalysis
Purpose:
  Deep analysis of two external tools (p-e-w/heretic and guillaumemeyer/watermarks-remover)
  mapped to SDD's existing governance and lifecycle frameworks. Demonstrates how
  SDD's capability chain and trust hierarchy handle security/privacy tools,
  including auto-blocking of censorship-removal tools and partial authorization
  of privacy tools.

Source: tmp/heretic/ (cloned 2026-09-01) + tmp/watermarks-remover/ (cloned 2026-09-01)
Trust Level: LEVEL 6 — EXTERNAL CONTENT

## 1. Project Overview

### Heretic (p-e-w/heretic)

Version: 2.0.0.dev0 | License: AGPLv3 | Author: Philipp Emanuel Weidmann

Heretic removes safety alignment ("censorship") from transformer-based language models
via directional ablation + TPE parameter optimization (Optuna). Supports dense models,
MoE, multimodal, and hybrid architectures.

Distribution: PyPI (`heretic-llm`), uv-managed, Python 3.10+, PyTorch 2.2+

Repository structure (9 source modules + 2 scorer plugins):

  src/heretic/
  ├── main.py          (1474 lines) — CLI entry, Optuna TPE optimizer loop
  ├── model.py         (867 lines)  — LoRA-based ablation, model loading
  ├── analyzer.py      (357 lines)  — Residual geometry, PaCMAP 2D plots
  ├── evaluator.py     (267 lines)  — Scorer plugin management
  ├── scorer.py        (68 lines)   — Abstract Scorer plugin base
  ├── config.py        (590 lines)  — Pydantic settings, ablation params
  ├── system.py        (478 lines)  — GPU/CPU detection, memory mgmt
  ├── reproduce.py     (391 lines)  — Reproducibility JSON, env verification
  ├── progress.py      (1314 bytes) — tqdm patching (disabled)
  ├── utils.py         (740 lines)  — Prompt handling, dataset loading
  ├── plugin.py        (305 lines)  — Plugin loader, Context safe API
  └── scorers/
      ├── keyword_rate.py  (138 lines) — Refusal keyword detection
      └── kl_divergence.py  (75 lines)  — KL divergence from baseline

Key dependencies: torch, transformers, huggingface-hub, optuna, peft,
bitsandbytes, accelerate, datasets, lm-eval, questionary, rich, pydantic-settings

### Watermarks-Remover (guillaumemeyer/watermarks-remover)

Version: v0.6.0 | License: MIT | Author: Guillaume Meyer

Agent skill + HTTP service to strip AI provenance marks from text and files.
Python 3.10+ stdlib service (no dependencies), with optional external backends.

Three-layer approach:
  Layer A (deterministic): Unicode/invisible chars, exotic spaces, bidi, tag chars
  Layer B (agent-driven): LLM-based rewrite for statistical watermarks
  File cleaners: C2PA/EXIF/XMP/props from 25+ file formats

Test suite: 50+ pytest tests covering input validation, symlink safety,
zip bombs, regex DoS (GHSA-7vpp-96qp-j9wh), PNG decompression bombs

