    code_path: service/scripts/clean_ctrlregen.py
    risk: HIGH — external backend, model download
    sdd_capability: system.modify + network.external (BLOCKED)

## 3. Capability Chain Analysis

### Heretic: Auto-BLOCKED by existing SDD policies

Heretic execution requires 4 things SDD already BLOCKS:

  1. model file access → @resource.model-files (MISSING — proposed below)
     → Would be classified CONFIDENTIAL per pattern @resource.system-files
     → CONFIDENTIAL resources excluded from AI context (RES-02)

  2. network.external → downloads models from HuggingFace
     → Code: main.py:50 `import huggingface_hub`
     → Code: reproduce.py:41 `api = HfApi()`
     → @capability.network.external — BLOCK at all autonomy levels L1-L5
     → Resource @resource.external-network — BLOCK always

  3. secret.access → needs HF API tokens for uploads
     → Code: main.py:1057 `huggingface_hub.get_token()`
     → Code: reproduce.py:62 `api.auth_check()`
     → @capability.secret.access — BLOCK at all levels
     → Resource @resource.secrets — RESTRICTED, never in context

  4. system.modify → install PyTorch/transformers/peft
     → Code: pyproject.toml dependencies (accelerate, bitsandbytes, datasets, etc.)
     → @capability.system.modify — BLOCK at L4/L5, HUMAN_ONLY at L3
     → Resource @resource.system-files — CONFIDENTIAL

**Conclusion: Heretic is auto-BLOCKED by existing SDD policies. NO new capabilities required for blocking.**

### Watermarks-Remover: Partially ALLOWED

Layer A (deterministic cleaning):
  - Uses: `@capability.code.read` + `@capability.code.write` (EXISTS, ALLOWED)
  - No external network, no secrets, no system modification
  - Security hardening already implemented (safe_arg, safe_write, size caps)

Layer B (optional backends):
  - `@capability.network.external` → BLOCKED (unless loopback-only)
  - `@capability.secret.access` → BLOCKED (API keys)
  - `@capability.system.modify` → BLOCKED (external backend install)

